[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186092315 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a3aefa5f-7730-50af-bdda-78228d7a1e41"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a3aefa5f-7730-50af-bdda-78228d7a1e41" :question/id #uuid "a3aefa5f-7730-50af-bdda-78228d7a1e41" :question/math-academy-id "q-143572" :question/problem "In a hardware store, there are three boxes containing light bulbs. Box $A$ contains $15$ bulbs, of which $2$ are defective. Box $B$ contains $10$ bulbs, of which $1$ is defective. And box $C$ contains $10$ light bulbs, of which $2$ are defective. A box is selected at random, and a bulb is randomly selected from the box. Find the probability that the bulb is defective." :question/worked-solution "Let $D$ be the event of selecting a defective bulb, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the bulb is from box $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the bulb is from box $B$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the bulb is from box $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space. \n\nTo calculate the probability of selecting a defective bulb at random from one of the three boxes, we can use the law of total probability: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap B)+P(D\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|B)P(B)+P(D|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since a box is selected at random, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=P(B)=P(C)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since there are $2$ defective bulbs out of $15$  in box $A,$ $1$ defective bulb out of $10$ in box $B,$ and $2$  defective bulbs out of $10$ bulbs in box $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nP(D|A)=\\frac{2}{15},\\,P(D|B)=\\frac{1}{10},\\,P(D|C)=\\frac{2}{10}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability of selecting a defective bulb at random from one of the three boxes is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|B)P(B)+P(D|C)P(C) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{15})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{1}{10})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{2}{10})(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{45}+\\frac{1}{30}+\\frac{2}{30} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{90}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-be770eee-142d-5138-82b0-d774ea34700b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-be770eee-142d-5138-82b0-d774ea34700b" :answer-field/id #uuid "be770eee-142d-5138-82b0-d774ea34700b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7f9ac3d1-fd3a-5663-99f5-0b6e86c9d756" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2091824b-6f43-593c-84fe-25de29e7e4e8" "answer-7f9ac3d1-fd3a-5663-99f5-0b6e86c9d756" "answer-4da788ef-fc41-5934-85c7-6c54e9d66986" "answer-8e788705-609a-5a7a-af02-0595198b67ae" "answer-8a76f1ca-01f8-5917-8e75-64c4de462b22"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2091824b-6f43-593c-84fe-25de29e7e4e8" :answer/id #uuid "2091824b-6f43-593c-84fe-25de29e7e4e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{85}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f9ac3d1-fd3a-5663-99f5-0b6e86c9d756" :answer/id #uuid "7f9ac3d1-fd3a-5663-99f5-0b6e86c9d756" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{90}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4da788ef-fc41-5934-85c7-6c54e9d66986" :answer/id #uuid "4da788ef-fc41-5934-85c7-6c54e9d66986" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21}{63}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e788705-609a-5a7a-af02-0595198b67ae" :answer/id #uuid "8e788705-609a-5a7a-af02-0595198b67ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23}{113}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a76f1ca-01f8-5917-8e75-64c4de462b22" :answer/id #uuid "8a76f1ca-01f8-5917-8e75-64c4de462b22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{38}{165}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092316 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-87509e91-72b0-5f1f-83b2-ad41631e8459"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-87509e91-72b0-5f1f-83b2-ad41631e8459" :question/id #uuid "87509e91-72b0-5f1f-83b2-ad41631e8459" :question/math-academy-id "q-144037" :question/problem "A cattle rancher has three ranches, where $34%$ of the rancher's cows are on ranch $A$, $36%$ are on ranch $B,$ and $30%$ on ranch $C.$ If $25%$ of all cows on ranch $A$ and $20%$ of all cows on ranch $B$ are dairy cows, and the probability that a randomly selected cow from any of the three ranches is a dairy cow is $37%,$ what is the probability that a randomly selected cow from ranch $C$ is a dairy cow?" :question/worked-solution "Let $D$ be the event that a selected cow is a dairy cow, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the cow is from ranch $A$,\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the cow is from ranch $B$,\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the cow is from ranch $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that the randomly selected cow is a dairy cow, we use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap B)+P(D\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|B)P(B)+P(D|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation. \n\n- Since $34%$ of all the rancher's cows are on ranch $A$, $36%$ are on ranch $B,$ and $30%$ are on ranch $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.34,\\,P(B)=0.36,\\,P(C)=0.3.\n$$\n\n- Since $25%$ of all cows on ranch $A$ and $20%$ of all cows on ranch $B$ are dairy cows, we have \n\n$$\nP(D|A)=0.25,\\,P(D|B)=0.2.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected cow from any of the three ranches is  a dairy cow is $37%,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(D)=0.37.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(D|C),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|B)P(B)+P(D|C)P(C) \\\\ 0.37 & =(0.25)(0.34)+(0.2)(0.36)+P(D|C)(0.3) \\\\ 0.37 & =0.085+0.072+0.3P(D|C) \\\\ 0.3P(D|C) & =0.213 \\\\ P(D|C) & =0.71\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected cow from ranch $C$ is a dairy cow is $71%.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e2414de2-0b71-5f21-ba04-5ccbaa91ec84"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e2414de2-0b71-5f21-ba04-5ccbaa91ec84" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2414de2-0b71-5f21-ba04-5ccbaa91ec84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4cd5ac84-c3f0-5b1e-9dc6-1b0238589e1d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-88aaed32-cbc4-5fb1-b688-7cc95b6f62b2" "answer-ce5f37d0-df7f-5e60-8207-efacf2cdc514" "answer-4cd5ac84-c3f0-5b1e-9dc6-1b0238589e1d" "answer-18462a6e-e5aa-5da9-9169-1897af9ddfc2" "answer-956129cb-062c-52cb-8b95-1feac6e6425c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88aaed32-cbc4-5fb1-b688-7cc95b6f62b2" :answer/id #uuid "88aaed32-cbc4-5fb1-b688-7cc95b6f62b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "59%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce5f37d0-df7f-5e60-8207-efacf2cdc514" :answer/id #uuid "ce5f37d0-df7f-5e60-8207-efacf2cdc514" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4cd5ac84-c3f0-5b1e-9dc6-1b0238589e1d" :answer/id #uuid "4cd5ac84-c3f0-5b1e-9dc6-1b0238589e1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "71%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18462a6e-e5aa-5da9-9169-1897af9ddfc2" :answer/id #uuid "18462a6e-e5aa-5da9-9169-1897af9ddfc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "74%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-956129cb-062c-52cb-8b95-1feac6e6425c" :answer/id #uuid "956129cb-062c-52cb-8b95-1feac6e6425c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "79%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-22ea1569-895b-50ca-99d6-870b4789bc76" :activity/id #uuid "22ea1569-895b-50ca-99d6-870b4789bc76" :activity/title "Ext