er-field/choices "answer-8e788705-609a-5a7a-af02-0595198b67ae"] ["answer-field-be770eee-142d-5138-82b0-d774ea34700b" :answer-field/choices "answer-8a76f1ca-01f8-5917-8e75-64c4de462b22"] ["question-a3aefa5f-7730-50af-bdda-78228d7a1e41" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-be770eee-142d-5138-82b0-d774ea34700b"] [17592186092315 :knowledge-point/questions "question-a3aefa5f-7730-50af-bdda-78228d7a1e41"] ["question-87509e91-72b0-5f1f-83b2-ad41631e8459" :question/id #uuid "87509e91-72b0-5f1f-83b2-ad41631e8459"] ["question-87509e91-72b0-5f1f-83b2-ad41631e8459" :question/math-academy-id "q-144037"] ["question-87509e91-72b0-5f1f-83b2-ad41631e8459" :question/problem "A cattle rancher has three ranches, where $34%$ of the rancher's cows are on ranch $A$, $36%$ are on ranch $B,$ and $30%$ on ranch $C.$ If $25%$ of all cows on ranch $A$ and $20%$ of all cows on ranch $B$ are dairy cows, and the probability that a randomly selected cow from any of the three ranches is a dairy cow is $37%,$ what is the probability that a randomly selected cow from ranch $C$ is a dairy cow?"] ["question-87509e91-72b0-5f1f-83b2-ad41631e8459" :question/worked-solution "Let $D$ be the event that a selected cow is a dairy cow, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the cow is from ranch $A$,\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the cow is from ranch $B$,\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the cow is from ranch $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that the randomly selected cow is a dairy cow, we use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap B)+P(D\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|B)P(B)+P(D|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation. \n\n- Since $34%$ of all the rancher's cows are on ranch $A$, $36%$ are on ranch $B,$ and $30%$ are on ranch $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.34,\\,P(B)=0.36,\\,P(C)=0.3.\n$$\n\n- Since $25%$ of all cows on ranch $A$ and $20%$ of all cows on ranch $B$ are dairy cows, we have \n\n$$\nP(D|A)=0.25,\\,P(D|B)=0.2.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected cow from any of the three ranches is  a dairy cow is $37%,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(D)=0.37.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(D|C),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|B)P(B)+P(D|C)P(C) \\\\ 0.37 & =(0.25)(0.34)+(0.2)(0.36)+P(D|C)(0.3) \\\\ 0.37 & =0.085+0.072+0.3P(D|C) \\\\ 0.3P(D|C) & =0.213 \\\\ P(D|C) & =0.71\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected cow from ranch $C$ is a dairy cow is $71%.$"] ["question-87509e91-72b0-5f1f-83b2-ad41631e8459" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-e2414de2-0b71-5f21-ba04-5ccbaa91ec84" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2414de2-0b71-5f21-ba04-5ccbaa91ec84"] ["answer-88aaed32-cbc4-5fb1-b688-7cc95b6f62b2" :answer/id #uuid "88aaed32-cbc4-5fb1-b688-7cc95b6f62b2"] ["answer-88aaed32-cbc4-5fb1-b688-7cc95b6f62b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-88aaed32-cbc4-5fb1-b688-7cc95b6f62b2" :answer/value "59%"] ["answer-ce5f37d0-df7f-5e60-8207-efacf2cdc514" :answer/id #uuid "ce5f37d0-df7f-5e60-8207-efacf2cdc514"] ["answer-ce5f37d0-df7f-5e60-8207-efacf2cdc514" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ce5f37d0-df7f-5e60-8207-efacf2cdc514" :answer/value "60%"] ["answer-4cd5ac84-c3f0-5b1e-9dc6-1b0238589e1d" :answer/id #uuid "4cd5ac84-c3f0-5b1e-9dc6-1b0238589e1d"] ["answer-4cd5ac84-c3f0-5b1e-9dc6-1b0238589e1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4cd5ac84-c3f0-5b1e-9dc6-1b0238589e1d" :answer/value "71%"] ["answer-18462a6e-e5aa-5da9-9169-1897af9ddfc2" :answer/id #uuid "18462a6e-e5aa-5da9-9169-1897af9ddfc2"] ["answer-18462a6e-e5aa-5da9-9169-1897af9ddfc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-18462a6e-e5aa-5da9-9169-1897af9ddfc2" :answer/value "74%"] ["answer-956129cb-062c-52cb-8b95-1feac6e6425c" :answer/id #uuid "956129cb-062c-52cb-8b95-1feac6e6425c